{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdiYNqW4EyYAScEMrhq6i","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I need approval to run `lethal.exe`. The command I want to run (from the working directory, in background):\n\n```\n./lethal.exe --project Cloud --tests Test --backend bcdev \\\n  --config lethal.config.envtool.json \\\n  --only \"Al/Codeunit/Codeunit 6175297 CDO Send Cust. Statement Mgt.al\" \\\n  --tests-only \"Src/AutomaticDocuments/**\" \\\n  --stop-hung-sessions --mutant-timeout-ms 180000\n```\n\nApprove it and I'll verify the new tests compile, go green, and report the score delta. Meanwhile, findings so far:\n\n**What the report says**\n\nScore 19.5% (25 killed + 1 timeout-killed, 107 survived, 15 no-coverage of 148).\n\nThe headline is not \"weak assertions\" — it is **one whole feature path has no tests at all**. `CreateOrSendAutStatements` (the `AUTSTATEMENT` branch of `OnRun`) is the only caller of `CreateAutomaticPeriodStatement`, `CreateAutomaticDueDateStatement`, `GetLastPerStatementSendingDate`, `GetLastStatementSendingDate`, `CheckForStatement`, `OpenEntriesInDueDatePeriod`, `EntriesInPeriod`, `CalcBalance`, `BalanceDue`. All of it is unreached. That is ~102 of the 122 non-killed mutants.\n\nThe 15 `no-coverage` mutants sit in `CreateOrSendAutStatements` itself. The other ~87 are labelled `survived` only because `coverageAttribution` is `\"object\"` — every mutant in the codeunit lists the same 9 covering tests, so \"survived\" here means \"some test touched the codeunit\", not \"a test executed this line\". Do not read those 87 as weak assertions.\n\nSecond thing worth telling the owner: `Tableextension 6175383 CDO Customer` lines 300–359 contain a near-verbatim copy of `CheckForStatement`/`EntriesInPeriod`/`CalcBalance`/`BalanceDue`. `CDO Aut Stat Bal Check Tests` tests *that* copy (via `Customer.CreateAutomaticPeriodStatement()`), which is why the logic looks covered while the codeunit's copy is not.\n\n**What I wrote** — `Test/Src/AutomaticDocuments/CDOAutStatementFeatureTests.Codeunit.al` (codeunit 68964), 19 tests:\n\n- 9 driving `CreateOrSendAutStatements` on the period-statement path — exact `Planned Sending Date`/`Start Date`/`End Date` assertions on the journal line (kills the `GetPeriodDates`/`CreateStatement` argument-swap and removal mutants), decoy e-mail-log rows differing in exactly one of template / table / customer / document type / zero planned date (kills the `SetRange` removals in `GetLastPerStatementSendingDate`), the `NextSendingDate = WorkDate` boundary, change-to-manual persistence, and the `Do not send if neg. balance` guard including the zero-balance boundary.\n- 4 on the due-date path — same treatment for `GetLastStatementSendingDate` and `OpenEntriesInDueDatePeriod` (`Open`, `Positive`, due-date range, customer filter).\n- 2 on `SendPeriodStatements` (manual customer skipped; manual switch persisted).\n- 3 on `ChangeAuatomaticToManual` (other customer's reminder, reminder posted *on* `LastDate`, reminder with only the finance-charge flag).\n- 3 on `IsCustomerStatementReport` (template usage filter, report-ID filter, the CDO Setup branch).\n\nTwo helpers detach leftover customers from earlier committed runs so each test only sees its own customer — `CreateOrSendAutStatements` commits inside its loop, so these tests cannot use `AutoRollback`, same constraint the existing suite already documents.\n\n**Survivors I deliberately did not chase**\n\n- `M0021`, `M0050`, `M0079`, `M0092`, `M0122` — `SetCurrentKey` removals. Ordering only; every one feeds an `IsEmpty` or a max-over-all-rows loop. Equivalent mutants.\n- `M0087`, `M0088`, `M0100`, `M0101` — `>` → `>=` inside `if x > Max then Max := x`. Provably the same result. Equivalent.\n- `M0060`, `M0067` — `CreateAutomaticPeriodStatement`'s return value is discarded at its only call site (line 98). Unobservable.\n- `M0104` — `exit(false)` when `not Cust.Get(CustomerNo)`; the customer came from the enclosing `FindSet`, so the branch is unreachable.\n- `M0004` — removing the `<>''` filter on `CDO Send Statement Code` is masked by `if SendCustStatement.Get(...)` on the next line.\n- `M0010` — `DOCustSetup.Find()` refreshes a row nothing has modified.\n- `M0012` — removing `Commit()` has no in-process observable effect.\n- `M0145` — `ReportNo > 0` → `>= 0` differs only when `ReportID = 0`, which is not a report.\n- `M0005`/`M0006` GUI dialog mutants and `M0074`–`M0076` (`Handle::\"E-Mail\"` → `SendMail`) — the first are unkillable under `GuiAllowed = No`; the second I left alone rather than have the suite attempt real mail sending. Worth flagging to the owner as a genuine coverage hole that needs a mail mock, not a test I should bolt on here."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":425,"cache_read_input_tokens":211890,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":425},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7f3c1a92-5d84-4b16-9e07-2c8a6f0d3b51","uuid":"01939a4b-6abb-40b0-99d0-75361d04baa2","timestamp":"2026-08-04T23:02:47.331Z","request_id":"req_011CdiYNmuG85rhWCvvBQrtT"}
